<title>USA: Putnam plans to insure money market funds.</title>
<headline>Putnam plans to insure money market funds.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Putnam Investments said it has arranged insurance to protect its money market funds against certain losses related to issuer default.</p>
<p>It said the insurance would guard against at least $30 million in aggregate losses for its five money market funds, which have assets of $2.3 billion.</p>
<p>Putnam is a unit of Marsh &amp; McLennan Cos Inc.</p>
</text>
